# reduce_scatter_test.cm
#
# In-network Reduce-Scatter over a 4-member group (one host per pod on a
# 16-host K=4 fat tree, so each member sits under a distinct ToR).
#
# The per-rank vector is 16384 bytes = 4 equal blocks of 4096 bytes. Every
# member emits its whole 16384-byte vector up the aggregation tree; the
# switches reduce each chunk independently; at the apex chunk/block i is
# delivered down to member group[i]:
#
#   block 0 -> host 0,  block 1 -> host 4,
#   block 2 -> host 8,  block 3 -> host 12
#
# Each member ends with its own 4096-byte slice. Completion (REDUCE_SCATTER_
# COMPLETE) fires once all 4 members have received their block.
#
# Requires: size divisible by |G| (16384 / 4 = 4096) and the resulting block
# size (4096) a multiple of the MTU (2048 or 4096) so no packet straddles a
# block boundary.
Nodes 16
Grp 0 4 8 12
Connections 1
0->0 id 1 start_reduce_scatter 0 size 16384
